course: dictionary
lesson: 3335
title: Finding evidence
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Evidence is facts, signs or objects that show something is true, or help to prove it. «There is no good evidence that cheese gives you nightmares.» When you read a claim like this, ask yourself what facts would show it is true. If nobody has found any, the claim is not proven.
explain: A detective looks for evidence: a muddy footprint, a torn letter, a witness who saw something. In science, evidence comes from tests and observations, and it backs up a conclusion. «Use evidence from the text» means point to the words in the text that prove your answer.
explain: Being an expert or being popular is not evidence. «Being related to an expert, or being popular, isn't evidence.» Good evidence is something you can check, such as a fact, a sign or a result.
fact: Evidence is a noun: facts, signs or objects that show something is true.
fact: In a court, evidence is what is shown to help decide whether someone did a crime.
fact: As a verb, «evidence» (formal) means to show or prove something.
fact: «No evidence» means there is nothing that proves the claim.
fact: «Scientific evidence» comes from careful tests and observations.
fact: Evidence is uncountable, so say «some evidence», not «an evidence».
exercise: «There is no good evidence that cheese gives you nightmares.» What does evidence mean here? | *Facts that show the claim is true | A bad dream | A kind of cheese
exercise: Which one is the best evidence that plants need water? | My friend says plants need water | *Plants given no water all week wilted, while watered ones stayed green | The plant has green leaves | The plant is in a pot
exercise: Mia says, «My uncle is a doctor, so my pills are safe.» What does the text say about this? | It is strong evidence | Doctors always know best | *Being related to an expert isn't evidence | Being popular is evidence
test: «Use evidence from the text to prove your answer.» What does this ask you to do? | Copy the whole text | Guess what you think | *Point to words in the text that show your answer is right | Draw a picture
test: Which phrase means nothing proves a claim? | *there is no evidence | find evidence | evidence of | there is evidence
exam: Ella says elephants are scared of mice because her gran said so. Is this good evidence? | Maybe, it depends on the mouse | *No, a claim is not proof, and there is no good evidence that elephants are especially afraid of mice | Yes, because elephants are big | Yes, grans always know best
